--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
WHAT THE WEB PAGE IS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SharingTripsPage.tsx is the "Share a trip" page. It reads useTrips({ vehicle_id,
limit: 20 }) (the recent trips, scoped to the selected vehicle) and renders, inside
a PageContainer (title + subtitle + loading), two GlassPanels:
  GlassPanel1 "Recent trips" — a role="listbox" of selectable role="option" rows.
    Loading shows three h-16 skeletons; an empty result shows an EmptyState (Route
    icon); each row shows a Route avatar, the trip name (or "Trip #id"), an
    InlineMetric(Calendar, formatDate(start)), an InlineMetric(Clock,
    formatDuration(start,end)), a "{{count}} drives" caption, the distance
    (MapPin, fmtInt(convertDistanceFromSI(total_distance_m)) + unit) and the energy
    (Zap, fmtNumber(total_energy_wh) + " Wh"). Clicking a row sets selectedTripId.
  GlassPanel2 "Static share cards" — a data-independent heading + body that points
    the user at the per-drive Share workflow.
A third FadeIn renders the propose-only AI share-card surface
(AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration), gated by
withAiFeature('trip-postcard-share-card-image-generation'); the page is
contractually required to keep working with AI OFF (ADR-015 §I3), and that AI-off
baseline is exactly these two panels.

The parity manifest scopes page:sharing/SharingTrips to dataSource useTrips, panels
[GlassPanel1, GlassPanel2], states [loading, empty, success], and 8 strings —
requiredCount 13. The AI card is its OWN parity unit
(shared-surfaces/AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration, already built) and is wired
by its own prompt with the SSE transport it needs; there is no production
TripImageDraftTransport in the tree yet (verified: zero call sites of
AITripPostcardShareCardImageGeneration(...) in src/main), so hosting it is out of
this page artifact's scope. This page still owns the selected-trip interaction the
AI surface consumes once hosted, so no parity is narrowed.

