NATIVE IMPLEMENTATION (no placeholders, ADR-011; no delegation)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
New files (package io.teslasync.android.sharing.sharingtrips, dir
apps/android/app/src/main/kotlin/com/teslasync/sharing/):
  - SharingTripsPageModel.kt   Registration (ROUTE_ID sharingTrips, WEB_PATH
                               /sharing/trips, SLUG SharingTripsPage, RECENT_LIMIT 20)
                               + SharingTripsDisplayPrefs (web useUnits: SI UnitPref +
                               locale; formatDistance via the shared SI converter ->
                               "1,234 mi"; formatEnergyWh -> verbatim watt-hours ->
                               "12,345.00 Wh") + sharingTripRow (per-row projection) +
                               formatTripDate (web formatDate -> "Apr 4, 2026") +
                               formatTripDuration (verbatim port of the web
                               start->end "2h 5m"/"45m"/"—") + recordSharingTrips
                               PageOpened (PII-safe view.opened, P1/S11). Pure /
                               framework-free, exercised by the testDebugUnitTest gate.
  - SharingTripsPageSource.kt  The data seam (selectedVehicleId / trips(params) /
                               settings) + sharingTripsPageSourceOf over the shared
                               S7 TripsRepository + SelectedVehicleStore + SettingsStore.
  - SharingTripsPageViewModel.kt  BaseFeedViewModel (P1/S8): tripsState =
                               combine(selectedVehicleId, refresh) flatMapLatest
                               trips(TripsParams(vehicleId, limit=20)) -> asUiState
                               (web useTrips, vehicle-scoped, empty -> UiPhase.Empty);
                               displayPrefs from the settings document; selectedTripId
                               + selectTrip (web selectedTripId useState); refresh/retry;
                               recordViewOpened.
  - SharingTripsPage.kt        Stateful entry (viewModel over the host-wired source,
                               records view.opened, collects tripsState + prefs +
                               selection) + stateless SharingTripsPageContent: the
                               header (PageTitle + subtitle + DataFreshness chip) over
                               RecentTripsPanel (GlassPanel1) and StaticShareCardsPanel
                               (GlassPanel2). GlassPanel1 switches the trips feed inline:
                               RecentTripsLoading (3 Skeletons) / RecentTripsError
                               (ErrorDisplay + retry) / RecentTripsEmpty (EmptyState,
                               Route) / RecentTripsList (selectableGroup of TripRow
                               Role.RadioButton rows, >=64dp, selection highlight). SI
                               values convert only here at the display boundary.
  - SharingTripsPageHost.kt    SharingTripsRoute() builds the source over
                               HttpTripsRepository(container.api, container.cacheStore)
                               + the container's selection/settings holders;
                               SharingTripsPageHost.register() -> PageHosts.register(
                               "sharingTrips"). Idempotent.

Edits (registration + ledger only):
  - TeslaSyncApplication.kt  import + SharingTripsPageHost.register() at process start
                             (after SqlPlaygroundPageHost.register()). The sharingTrips
                             /sharing/trips destination already exists in Destinations.kt
                             (NavGroup.Sharing) — host wiring only (the "NavHost
                             registration" allowed file).
  - apps/parity/android-ledger.json  page:sharing/SharingTrips row (done, 13/13).

Notes:
  - i18n: all 8 keys already exist in the AUTO-GENERATED res/values/strings.xml
    (translation_sharing_trips_*), so strings.xml was NOT modified. Every visible
    literal resolves via stringResource (ADR-014); web key names kept. The only
    non-stringResource text is the unit token suffix ("mi"/"km"/"Wh"), which is a
    display-boundary unit label sourced from UnitPref — exactly as the web row reads
    unitPrefs.distance and the literal "Wh" — not translatable UI copy.
  - SI (Phase-48): trips arrive SI-canonical; total_distance_m converts to the user's
    unit via the shared SI converter (formatDistance(meters, units, 0)); total_energy_wh
    renders verbatim in watt-hours (web fmtNumber(total_energy_wh) + " Wh"); nothing is
    stored/computed non-SI.
  - States: loading (skeletons) / empty (EmptyState) / success (selectable rows) are
    the 3 manifest states; a hard error additionally renders ErrorDisplay + Retry
    (UiState.isError, no cached fallback), and a cache-served stale/offline tier is
    surfaced by the header DataFreshness chip — no region ever blanks (ADR-011/ADR-013).
  - Live data: useTrips is cache-then-network, NOT an SSE feed, so there is no >2-min
    live-staleness pill (ADR-013); the DataFreshness chip carries stale/offline/error.
  - a11y: PageTitle heading; the recent list is a selectableGroup with a
    contentDescription; each row is a Role.RadioButton selection target >=64dp with the
    selected state announced; decorative glyphs pass contentDescription=null (ADR-015).
    Dynamic-color / dark theme via MaterialTheme tokens (no hardcoded colors).
  - The AI share-card region is a separate parity unit with no production transport in
    the tree; not hosted here (honest scope, covenant #2 — the manifest's 13 items are
    fully covered). The selection model that feeds it IS implemented.

